@startuml
title TriggerIQ ERP - High-Level Architecture with CBAM

' Participants
rectangle "ERP Core Modules" as ERP {
  [Inventory Module]
  [Sales Module]
  [Finance Module]
  [Procurement Module]
}

rectangle "AI / ML" as AI {
  [AI Recommender]
  [Chatbot]
}

rectangle "Blockchain Ledger" as BC {
  [Immutable Transaction Log]
  [Smart Contracts]
}

rectangle "External Systems" as EXT {
  [Suppliers]
  [Customers]
  [Banks / Payment Gateways]
}

rectangle "CBAM Evaluation Layer" as CBAM {
  [Cost Analysis]
  [Benefit Assessment]
  [Trade-off Decisions]
}

database "ERP Database" as DB

cloud "CI/CD & Monitoring" as CI

' --- High-Level Flow ---
EXT --> ERP: Orders / Goods / Payments
ERP --> DB: Store transactions, inventory, invoices
ERP --> BC: Record transactions / smart contracts
AI --> ERP: Forecast, recommendations
ERP --> AI: Provide ERP data

' --- CBAM Layer ---
ERP --> CBAM: Send performance & cost metrics
AI --> CBAM: Send predictions & ROI estimates
CBAM --> ERP: Inform prioritization & trade-offs

ERP --> CI: Logs, monitoring
BC --> CI: Blockchain audit logs

' Notes
note right of CBAM
CBAM continuously evaluates:
- Cost of features
- Benefit of automation
- ROI of AI + Blockchain
- Security trade-offs
end note

note left of AI
AI forecasts demand, predicts trends,
recommends inventory & pricing
end note

note left of BC
Blockchain ensures immutability
and traceable transactions
end note

@enduml